[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-64515"] :question/problem "Let $y={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}$ be a series solution to the equation ${y}^{″}-y=0.$  Find $f(n),$ given that the recurrence relation for ${a}_{n}$ can be written as\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+2}=\\frac{{a}_{n}}{f(n)},\\,n=0,1,2…\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${y}^{′}(x)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & ={({\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n})}^{′} \\\\  & ={({a}_{0}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n})}^{′} \\\\  & =0+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, we find ${y}^{″}(x)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{″}(x) & ={({\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1})}^{′} \\\\  & ={({a}_{1}+{\\sum }_{n=2}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1})}^{′} \\\\  & =0+{\\sum }_{n=2}^{\\infty }n(n-1){a}_{n}{x}^{n-2} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=2}^{\\infty }n(n-1){a}_{n}{x}^{n-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute the expressions for $y(x)$ and ${y}^{″}(x)$ into the given differential equation:\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=2}^{\\infty }n(n-1){a}_{n}{x}^{n-2}-{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}=0\n$$\n\nWe want to make the powers of $x$ the same. Therefore, in the first sum, we change the index of the summation by writing $m=n-2.$ This gives\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{m=0}^{\\infty }(m+2)(m+1){a}_{m+2}{x}^{m}-{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}=0.\n$$\n\nReplacing $m$ with $n$ in the first summation (since it does not matter which letter we use) gives\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }(n+2)(n+1){a}_{n+2}{x}^{n}-{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}=0.\n$$\n\nSince both sums now start with $n=0,$ we can combine them as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }[(n+2)(n+1){a}_{n+2}-{a}_{n}]{x}^{n}=0\n$$\n\nSetting each coefficient of $x$ equal to zero, we obtain\n\n$$\n(n+2)(n+1){a}_{n+2}-{a}_{n}=0.\n$$\n\nFinally then, the recursion formula is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+2}=\\frac{{a}_{n}}{(n+1)(n+2)},\\,n=0,1,2…\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(n)=(n+1)(n+2).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-101389/selection/a1fcd330294d042366b496e426a7c8cac554a6c2df4fa4497f3218868ee5e877" :answer/id #uuid "151db3f9-258e-5d5b-b887-b6ace8346d3e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(n)=2n(n+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101389/selection/1acc8a783ccbfae6a4ff0c7cdceed7a337d3c8ff9937ad19eb4a9bf5be764cdb" :answer/id #uuid "563dbd2e-ece6-50cd-9efb-c52e41d8e252" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(n)=-\\frac{(n+1)(n+2)}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101389/selection/a441bd67f917c7eb96cb57e1104b9f3a321f89a0914cd45a9608a71fb7144e62" :answer/id #uuid "4799e5ad-19e2-55fc-8842-686df215e6b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(n)=2(n+1)(n+2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101389/selection/6f3ef05909080f6c212f68b71ed3058468ebaf8c5fa15b55eae63a00a6aca857" :answer/id #uuid "1b33b297-5e39-5b84-9c11-20bad5561b7a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(n)=\\frac{(n+1)(n+2)}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101389/selection/1962df074d98e79e42dcb50c3f789c8449e4d420267cde034e02b4a72f03676d" :answer/id #uuid "1602d4cf-6f96-55a1-9aa5-af0e750fffaa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "f(n)=-2(n+1)(n+2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101389/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ccc29b0b-638a-5b35-a5d4-a57711a38aac" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-101389/selection/a441bd67f917c7eb96cb57e1104b9f3a321f89a0914cd45a9608a71fb7144e62" :answer-field/choices ["q-101389/selection/a1fcd330294d042366b496e426a7c8cac554a6c2df4fa4497f3218868ee5e877" "q-101389/selection/1acc8a783ccbfae6a4ff0c7cdceed7a337d3c8ff9937ad19eb4a9bf5be764cdb" "q-101389/selection/a441bd67f917c7eb96cb57e1104b9f3a321f89a0914cd45a9608a71fb7144e62" "q-101389/selection/6f3ef05909080f6c212f68b71ed3058468ebaf8c5fa15b55eae63a00a6aca857" "q-101389/selection/1962df074d98e79e42dcb50c3f789c8449e4d420267cde034e02b4a72f03676d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-101389" :question/id #uuid "b5bd1188-011f-5de8-8224-47cb9fd29c4b" :question/math-academy-id "q-101389" :question/problem "Let $y={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}$ be a series solution to the equation $18{y}^{″}-9y=0.$  Find $f(n),$ given that the recurrence relation for ${a}_{n}$ can be written as\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+2}=\\frac{{a}_{n}}{f(n)},\\,n=0,1,2…\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${y}^{′}(x)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & ={({\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n})}^{′} \\\\  & ={({a}_{0}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n})}^{′} \\\\  & =0+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, we find ${y}^{″}(x)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{″}(x) & ={({\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1})}^{′} \\\\  & ={({a}_{1}+{\\sum }_{n=2}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1})}^{′} \\\\  & =0+{\\sum }_{n=2}^{\\infty }n(n-1){a}_{n}{x}^{n-2} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=2}^{\\infty }n(n-1){a}_{n}{x}^{n-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute the expressions for $y(x)$ and ${y}^{″}(x)$ into the given differential equation:\n\n$$\n18{\\sum }_{n=2}^{\\infty }n(n-1){a}_{n}{x}^{n-2}-9{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}=0\n$$\n\nWe want to make the powers of $x$ the same. Therefore, in the first sum, we change the index of the summation by writing $m=n-2.$ This gives\n\n$$\n18{\\sum }_{m=0}^{\\infty }(m+2)(m+1){a}_{m+2}{x}^{m}-9{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}=0.\n$$\n\nReplacing $m$ with $n$ in the first summation (since it does not matter which letter we use) gives\n\n$$\n18{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }(n+2)(n+1){a}_{n+2}{x}^{n}-9{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}=0.\n$$\n\nSince both sums now start with $n=0,$ we can combine them as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }[18(n+2)(n+1){a}_{n+2}-9{a}_{n}]{x}^{n}=0\n$$\n\nSetting each coefficient of $x$ equal to zero, we obtain\n\n$$\n18(n+2)(n+1){a}_{n+2}-9{a}_{n}=0.\n$$\n\nFinally then, the recursion formula is\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+2}=\\frac{{a}_{n}}{2(n+1)(n+2)},\\,n=0,1,2…\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(n)=2(n+1)(n+2).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-101389/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1980ddeb-37bf-5234-8888-f8292e2c9405"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-101389"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-101403/selection/9e8f3d7c434511bd46ffa2512cb3145c0eefbb3133bd4f9271bc50cbfe2d2e66" :answer/id #uuid "3303e07a-ba8e-5b03-b423-d30ca1b4908a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{2{a}_{n-1}}{5(n+1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101403/selection/af918cbf91876245139af34af059863f647261f79e7d894062b0650f43071355" :answer/id #uuid "234f91be-a0ab-557d-9ca2-cde2074029b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{{a}_{n}}{5n+2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101403/selection/9f8fb6655d7bb67d31cfa52a543123e628ba4c811fbb152613f3f810e1c1aa0f" :answer/id #uuid "badd6234-c1a5-5521-8a70-271e206dd05c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{{a}_{n-1}}{5(n+1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101403/selection/4c1ab00abf52396c350495bbbcabb04755590a07922b488b29fd32812faf3d9c" :answer/id #uuid "050a1396-0a09-55cb-96b9-e4be221a86fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{5{a}_{n}}{2(n+1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101403/selection/8767b6c40f4a86007b4559ed9a81136dc1fb4271bc13534a22f722ca9c34fe71" :answer/id #uuid "6b8f18fc-83b2-5020-93c4-f82f0a57f697" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=10{a}_{n}(n+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-101403/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6e663ad7-1dab-574f-a964-40d082646d40" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-101403/selection/9e8f3d7c434511bd46ffa2512cb3145c0eefbb3133bd4f9271bc50cbfe2d2e66" :answer-field/choices ["q-101403/selection/9e8f3d7c434511bd46ffa2512cb3145c0eefbb3133bd4f9271bc50cbfe2d2e66" "q-101403/selection/af918cbf91876245139af34af059863f647261f79e7d894062b0650f43071355" "q-101403/selection/9f8fb6655d7bb67d31cfa52a543123e628ba4c811fbb152613f3f810e1c1aa0f" "q-101403/selection/4c1ab00abf52396c350495bbbcabb04755590a07922b488b29fd32812faf3d9c" "q-101403/selection/8767b6c40f4a86007b4559ed9a81136dc1fb4271bc13534a22f722ca9c34fe71"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-101403" :question/id #uuid "b4a15be5-56fd-581a-a9cd-9c8be7b9791e" :question/math-academy-id "q-101403" :question/problem "Let $y={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}$ be a series solution to the equation $5{y}^{′}-2xy=0.$\n\nWhat is the recurrence relation for the coefficients ${a}_{n},$ where $n=1,2,3,…$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${y}^{′}(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & ={({\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n})}^{′} \\\\  & ={({a}_{0}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n})}^{′} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute the expressions for $y(x)$ and ${y}^{′}(x)$ into the given differential equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1}-2x{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n} & =0 \\\\ {\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }5n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1}-{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }2{a}_{n}{x}^{n+1} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe want to make the powers of $x$ the same. Therefore, in the first sum, we change the index of the summation by writing $m=n-1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{m=0}^{\\infty }5(m+1){a}_{m+1}{x}^{m}-{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }2{a}_{n}{x}^{n+1}=0.\n$$\n\nNow, in the second series, we change the index of the summation by writing $m=n+1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{m=0}^{\\infty }5(m+1){a}_{m+1}{x}^{m}-{\\sum }_{m=1}^{\\infty }2{a}_{m-1}{x}^{m}=0.\n$$\n\nReplacing $m$ with $n$ in both summations (since it does not matter which letter we use) gives\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }5(n+1){a}_{n+1}{x}^{n}-{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }2{a}_{n-1}{x}^{n}=0.\n$$\n\nNext, we need to get two series starting with the same value of $n.$ So, we take out the term $n=0$ from the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n5{a}_{1}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }5(n+1){a}_{n+1}{x}^{n}-{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }2{a}_{n-1}{x}^{n}=0\n$$\n\nWe now combine the series, as follows:\n\n$$\n5{a}_{1}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }[5(n+1){a}_{n+1}-2{a}_{n-1}]{x}^{n}=0\n$$\n\nFinally, by equating coefficients of ${x}^{n},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=0,\\,5(n+1){a}_{n+1}=2{a}_{n-1}.\n$$\n\nSolving for ${a}_{n+1}$ gives\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{2{a}_{n-1}}{5(n+1)},\\,n=1,2,3,….\n$$\n\nNote that every coefficient with an odd index is equal to $0,$ since ${a}_{1}=0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-101403/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37ab3f10-aca4-5094-98d2-0de9c11fd711"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-101403"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-102315/selection/05b0774cfe5d1abe46a45c3479b767e852e7d0f8fca98307a1d161a2371abe80" :answer/id #uuid "4ab77680-db2f-5819-961b-2d868d057602" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{{a}_{n-1}}{9(n+1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102315/selection/33377fdb54b01727f8e95b8ccbb7c370e3641626ff4b2149b6a51c063c39ec9c" :answer/id #uuid "3a067f6b-3a66-577b-987e-a04ed4cd85ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{{a}_{n-1}}{9n+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102315/selection/7ac955fb51f0189548117640bbd66a4c2dae19209e6fab238b23a6e904e3d5dc" :answer/id #uuid "2155f10e-a88d-5885-8ceb-f8baa45f3603" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=-\\frac{{a}_{n-1}}{9(n+1)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102315/selection/6417771413f3d7bfed04878725f067815fec38b302cddb0485e52e85693ff667" :answer/id #uuid "0abd4e93-6c73-5a00-b2f1-3b79c4965074" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=-9{a}_{n-1}(n+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102315/selection/d019d6d0e70bacb0b74b424039ca64bb71aca4d85e74d2f1c2d104457687b4f7" :answer/id #uuid "ad71331c-fca7-592e-9d2c-7ad49bd3901c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=-\\frac{{a}_{n-1}}{9n+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-102315/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "fdae2540-94a1-5d66-8c47-0d41668d85d7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-102315/selection/7ac955fb51f0189548117640bbd66a4c2dae19209e6fab238b23a6e904e3d5dc" :answer-field/choices ["q-102315/selection/05b0774cfe5d1abe46a45c3479b767e852e7d0f8fca98307a1d161a2371abe80" "q-102315/selection/33377fdb54b01727f8e95b8ccbb7c370e3641626ff4b2149b6a51c063c39ec9c" "q-102315/selection/7ac955fb51f0189548117640bbd66a4c2dae19209e6fab238b23a6e904e3d5dc" "q-102315/selection/6417771413f3d7bfed04878725f067815fec38b302cddb0485e52e85693ff667" "q-102315/selection/d019d6d0e70bacb0b74b424039ca64bb71aca4d85e74d2f1c2d104457687b4f7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-102315" :question/id #uuid "9acbfa33-35c8-5eb4-af30-be51fe0a0220" :question/math-academy-id "q-102315" :question/problem "Let $y={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}$ be a series solution to the equation $xy+9{y}^{′}=0.$\n\nWhat is the recurrence relation for the coefficients ${a}_{n},$ where $n=1,2,3,…$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${y}^{′}(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & ={({\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n})}^{′} \\\\  & ={({a}_{0}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n})}^{′} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute the expressions for $y(x)$ and ${y}^{′}(x)$ into the given differential equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}+9{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1} & =0 \\\\ {\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n+1}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }9n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe want to make the powers of $x$ the same. Therefore, in the second sum, we change the index of the summation by writing $m=n-1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n+1}+{\\sum }_{m=0}^{\\infty }9(m+1){a}_{m+1}{x}^{m}=0.\n$$\n\nNow, in the first series, we change the index of the summation by writing $m=n+1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{m=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{m-1}{x}^{m}+{\\sum }_{m=0}^{\\infty }9(m+1){a}_{m+1}{x}^{m}=0.\n$$\n\nReplacing $m$ with $n$ in both summations (since it does not matter which letter we use) gives\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n-1}{x}^{n}+{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }9(n+1){a}_{n+1}{x}^{n}=0.\n$$\n\nNext, we need to get two series starting with the same value of $n.$ So, we take out the term $n=0$ from the right-hand side:\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n-1}{x}^{n}+9{a}_{1}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }9(n+1){a}_{n+1}{x}^{n}=0\n$$\n\nWe now combine the series, as follows:\n\n$$\n9{a}_{1}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }[{a}_{n-1}+9(n+1){a}_{n+1}]{x}^{n}=0\n$$\n\nFinally, by equating coefficients of ${x}^{n},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=0,\\,9(n+1){a}_{n+1}=-{a}_{n-1}.\n$$\n\nSolving for ${a}_{n+1}$ gives\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=-\\frac{{a}_{n-1}}{9(n+1)},\\,n=1,2,3,….\n$$\n\nNote that every coefficient with an odd index is equal to $0,$ since ${a}_{1}=0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-102315/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37ab3f10-aca4-5094-98d2-0de9c11fd711"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-102315"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-365776/selection/247f23996a84d4c1da595046e085e51649196a41822f88a80a57a0a99255180f" :answer/id #uuid "7b1152e6-383e-5d08-abe6-97bf69210f0e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{-2{a}_{n-1}}{n+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365776/selection/25687c4903f0602494eb4c2d8ecce6251e3e1ef32f3be4636728f80e9bad32d6" :answer/id #uuid "48be2863-d777-5985-a3e8-e70c96674496" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=-2{a}_{n}(n+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365776/selection/e7a699f99512edb2bd6389d06e8d918062e32a6d335427eace2090f36ea39aa0" :answer/id #uuid "d9845efa-ee87-53ff-bd51-26f4dcda4dbc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{-2{a}_{n-1}}{n}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365776/selection/a66a0e973784c2963b82272191583203323f12f1397a9a267f70536bfd4fa8ac" :answer/id #uuid "635e5672-d098-5348-9c7d-4c8d0e0d0cc3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{2{a}_{n-1}}{n+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365776/selection/9c65f513e1fa42a416382f1b88f615ddb25191480b85ff66803de015e3d73f4a" :answer/id #uuid "50cb3ecf-79d9-5218-8159-ad90d4b8e074" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{-2{a}_{n}}{n+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-365776/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5259d813-0292-5c81-95f1-2971bcdd7542" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-365776/selection/247f23996a84d4c1da595046e085e51649196a41822f88a80a57a0a99255180f" :answer-field/choices ["q-365776/selection/247f23996a84d4c1da595046e085e51649196a41822f88a80a57a0a99255180f" "q-365776/selection/25687c4903f0602494eb4c2d8ecce6251e3e1ef32f3be4636728f80e9bad32d6" "q-365776/selection/e7a699f99512edb2bd6389d06e8d918062e32a6d335427eace2090f36ea39aa0" "q-365776/selection/a66a0e973784c2963b82272191583203323f12f1397a9a267f70536bfd4fa8ac" "q-365776/selection/9c65f513e1fa42a416382f1b88f615ddb25191480b85ff66803de015e3d73f4a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-365776" :question/id #uuid "01e4a118-39ab-5f83-a84a-4e3bea205b9e" :question/math-academy-id "q-365776" :question/problem "Let $y={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}$ be a series solution to the equation ${y}^{′}+2xy=0.$\n\nWhat is the recurrence relation for the coefficients ${a}_{n},$ where $n=1,2,3…$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${y}^{′}(x)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & ={({\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n})}^{′} \\\\  & ={({a}_{0}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n})}^{′} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we substitute the expressions for $y(x)$ and ${y}^{′}(x)$ into the given differential equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1}+2x{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n} & =0 \\\\ {\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }n{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1}+{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }2{a}_{n}{x}^{n+1} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe want to make the powers of $x$ the same. Therefore, in the first sum, we change the index of the summation by writing $m=n-1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{m=0}^{\\infty }(m+1){a}_{m+1}{x}^{m}+{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }2{a}_{n}{x}^{n+1}=0.\n$$\n\nNow, in the second series, we change the index of the summation by writing $m=n+1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{m=0}^{\\infty }(m+1){a}_{m+1}{x}^{m}+{\\sum }_{m=1}^{\\infty }2{a}_{m-1}{x}^{m}=0.\n$$\n\nReplacing $m$ with $n$ in both summations (since it does not matter which letter we use) gives\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }(n+1){a}_{n+1}{x}^{n}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }2{a}_{n-1}{x}^{n}=0.\n$$\n\nNext, we need to get two series starting with the same value of $n.$ So, we take out the term $n=0$ from the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }(n+1){a}_{n+1}{x}^{n}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }2{a}_{n-1}{x}^{n}=0\n$$\n\nWe now combine the series, as follows:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }[(n+1){a}_{n+1}+2{a}_{n-1}]{x}^{n}=0\n$$\n\nFinally, by equating coefficients of ${x}^{n},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=0,\\,(n+1){a}_{n+1}=-2{a}_{n-1}.\n$$\n\nSolving for ${a}_{n+1}$ gives\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=\\frac{-2{a}_{n-1}}{n+1},\\,n=1,2,3….\n$$\n\nNote that every coefficient with an odd index is equal to $0,$ since ${a}_{1}=0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-365776/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "37ab3f10-aca4-5094-98d2-0de9c11fd711"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-365776"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
